## Context

Figure 3 of the arXiv preprint (slides/manuscript/main.md) is
`fig_exp2_arms_comparison.pdf`, generated by
`src/aedist/plot_exp2_arms_comparison.py`. The two-panel comparison figure
shows coverage (left) and cost (right) for the four Exp2 arms (1N/5N/1D/5D)
but does NOT include the Exp1 memory-only parametric baseline bar.

The sibling script `plot_exp2_arms_split.py` already draws a hatched "E1"
baseline bar using `load_exp1_summary()` from `aedist.exp1_cost_quality`.
Author directive 2026-06-08: the comparison figure must show the same Exp1
baseline for naive-vs-optimised-vs-memory context.

## Relevant files

- `src/aedist/plot_exp2_arms_comparison.py` — target script (two-panel figure)
- `src/aedist/plot_exp2_arms_split.py` — reference implementation (has E1 bar)
- `src/aedist/exp1_cost_quality.py` — shared library for Exp1 summary data
- `report/inputs/generated/fig_exp2_arms_comparison.pdf` — committed artifact
- `experiments/render.mk` — Makefile rule for the figure
- `tests/test_plot_exp2_arms_comparison.py` — existing tests

## Actions

1. Add `_AGENT_EXP1_SLUG` map and 5-bar layout (E1 + 4 arms) to comparison script.
2. Import `load_cost_quality_rows`, `summary_by_slug` from `exp1_cost_quality`.
3. Add `load_exp1_summary()` helper (mirrors split script).
4. Draw E1 hatched bar in both coverage and cost panels.
5. Update `make_figure` signature to accept exp1_summary.
6. Rebuild PDF via Makefile target; verify E1 appears via pdftotext.
7. Add integration test confirming E1 summary loads and bar renders.

## Test

- pdftotext of rebuilt PDF contains "E1" label for each agent group.
- PDF size grows (baseline: 32063 bytes) due to additional bars.
- `make check-fast` and `pytest -m adherence` pass.

## Verification

- [ ] E1 hatched bars visible in coverage panel for all 4 agents
- [ ] E1 hatched bars visible in cost panel for all 4 agents
- [ ] E1 bar labels ("E1") appear in pdftotext output
- [ ] PDF size > baseline (32063 bytes)
- [ ] `make check-fast` green
- [ ] `pytest -m adherence` green

## Invariants

- Two-panel layout preserved (coverage + cost)
- Existing Exp2 arm bars unchanged
- N_REFERENCE_PLANTS via reference_plant_count(), no hardcoded literals
- Makefile DAG unchanged (same target, same prerequisites)

## Exit criteria

- Figure 3 shows the Exp1 memory-only baseline bar (hatched, E1 label)
  in both coverage and cost panels for all four agents.
- Rebuilt PDF committed. Tests green.
